@*
 * FILE ROLE: Admin area _ViewStart.cshtml — sets the default layout for all views
 *   inside Areas/Admin/Views/**. Because the Admin area has its own
 *   Areas/Admin/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml, the "_Layout" reference resolves to the
 *   area-specific layout rather than the root Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml.
 *
 * SECTION 13: AREA _ViewStart.cshtml
 *
 * _ViewStart.cshtml SCOPING IN AREAS:
 *   The framework applies _ViewStart.cshtml files hierarchically from most general
 *   to most specific. For Areas/Admin/Views/Dashboard/Index.cshtml:
 *     1. _ViewStart.cshtml (project root)              — applied first (if exists)
 *     2. Areas/_ViewStart.cshtml                       — applied next (if exists)
 *     3. Areas/Admin/_ViewStart.cshtml                 — applied next (if exists)
 *     4. Areas/Admin/Views/_ViewStart.cshtml           ← this file
 *     5. Areas/Admin/Views/Dashboard/_ViewStart.cshtml — applied last (if exists)
 *   Later files override earlier ones. This file overrides any project-root default.
 *
 * WHY AREAS NEED THEIR OWN _ViewStart:
 *   If there were only a root Views/_ViewStart.cshtml, it would NOT be picked up
 *   by area views (the discovery path for area views walks through Areas/, not Views/).
 *   Each area needs its own _ViewStart.cshtml in Areas/{area}/Views/ to assign a layout.
 *
 * "_Layout" RESOLUTION FOR ADMIN AREA VIEWS:
 *   Layout = "_Layout" triggers the layout discovery order:
 *     1. Areas/Admin/Views/Dashboard/_Layout.cshtml     — not found
 *     2. Areas/Admin/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml        ← FOUND — Admin area layout
 *   The Admin area uses its own custom layout (different header colour/branding).
 *
 * OPTING OUT OF LAYOUT IN A SPECIFIC VIEW:
 *   @{ Layout = null; }   — disable layout for this view only
 *   @{ Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml"; }  — force root layout from area view
*@

@{
    Layout = "_Layout"; // resolves to Areas/Admin/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml
}
